{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function debounce<TFn>(fn, initialOptions): (...args) => void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/pacer/src/debouncer.ts#L328","children":[{"type":"text","value":"debouncer.ts:328"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a debounced function that delays invoking the provided function until after a specified wait time.\nMultiple calls during the wait period will cancel previous pending invocations and reset the timer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This synchronous version is lighter weight and often all you need - upgrade to asyncDebounce when you need promises, retry support, abort/cancel capabilities, or advanced error handling."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If leading option is true, the function will execute immediately on the first call, then wait the delay\nbefore allowing another execution."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uses TanStack Store for reactive state management"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState"},{"type":"text","value":" to provide initial state values when creating the debouncer"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onExecute"},{"type":"text","value":" callback to react to function execution and implement custom logic"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The state includes canLeadingExecute, execution count, and isPending status"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State can be accessed via the underlying Debouncer instance's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"store.state"},{"type":"text","value":" property"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When using framework adapters (React/Solid), state is accessed from the hook's state property"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/AnyFunction.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyFunction"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"initialoptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"initialOptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/DebouncerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DebouncerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(..."},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"args"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const debounced = debounce(() => {\n  saveChanges();\n}, { wait: 1000 });\n\n// Called repeatedly but executes at most once per second\ninputElement.addEventListener('input', debounced);","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfn","text":"TFn","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"initialoptions","text":"initialOptions","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction debounce<TFn>(fn, initialOptions): (...args) => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [debouncer.ts:328](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/pacer/src/debouncer.ts#L328)\n\nCreates a debounced function that delays invoking the provided function until after a specified wait time.\nMultiple calls during the wait period will cancel previous pending invocations and reset the timer.\n\nThis synchronous version is lighter weight and often all you need - upgrade to asyncDebounce when you need promises, retry support, abort/cancel capabilities, or advanced error handling.\n\nIf leading option is true, the function will execute immediately on the first call, then wait the delay\nbefore allowing another execution.\n\nState Management:\n- Uses TanStack Store for reactive state management\n- Use `initialState` to provide initial state values when creating the debouncer\n- Use `onExecute` callback to react to function execution and implement custom logic\n- The state includes canLeadingExecute, execution count, and isPending status\n- State can be accessed via the underlying Debouncer instance's `store.state` property\n- When using framework adapters (React/Solid), state is accessed from the hook's state property\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* [`AnyFunction`](../type-aliases/AnyFunction.md)\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### initialOptions\n\n[`DebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/DebouncerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(...`args`) => `void`\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst debounced = debounce(() => {\n  saveChanges();\n}, { wait: 1000 });\n\n// Called repeatedly but executes at most once per second\ninputElement.addEventListener('input', debounced);\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: debounce\ntitle: debounce\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction debounce<TFn>(fn, initialOptions): (...args) => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [debouncer.ts:328](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/pacer/src/debouncer.ts#L328)\n\nCreates a debounced function that delays invoking the provided function until after a specified wait time.\nMultiple calls during the wait period will cancel previous pending invocations and reset the timer.\n\nThis synchronous version is lighter weight and often all you need - upgrade to asyncDebounce when you need promises, retry support, abort/cancel capabilities, or advanced error handling.\n\nIf leading option is true, the function will execute immediately on the first call, then wait the delay\nbefore allowing another execution.\n\nState Management:\n- Uses TanStack Store for reactive state management\n- Use `initialState` to provide initial state values when creating the debouncer\n- Use `onExecute` callback to react to function execution and implement custom logic\n- The state includes canLeadingExecute, execution count, and isPending status\n- State can be accessed via the underlying Debouncer instance's `store.state` property\n- When using framework adapters (React/Solid), state is accessed from the hook's state property\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* [`AnyFunction`](../type-aliases/AnyFunction.md)\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### initialOptions\n\n[`DebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/DebouncerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(...`args`) => `void`\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst debounced = debounce(() => {\n  saveChanges();\n}, { wait: 1000 });\n\n// Called repeatedly but executes at most once per second\ninputElement.addEventListener('input', debounced);\n```\n"}
